From 231afc66c3a742a8dcb73d8b948d7fd6b7dd9cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: indextree <hellonypcteam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:41:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Fix Fiat-Shamir: chained transcript bound to circuit,
 public I/O and all messages

Upstream derived each sumcheck challenge as MiMC(current round polynomial) and
r* as MiMC(last round polynomial) only, and fixed the output point z0 = 0 (only
output gate 0 was ever checked). Challenges were therefore independent of the
circuit, the public input/output, the claim and all earlier messages.

- new gkr::transcript: Transcript trait + MimcTranscript (circomlib
  MultiMiMC7-compatible sponge-like chain; in-crate MiMC7, mimc-rs (GPL) only
  as a test-only cross-check)
- statement absorbed first: circuit digest (depth, k list, every add/mult
  gate), input values, output values; z0 squeezed from the transcript
- every round polynomial normalized to 3 coefficients and absorbed before its
  challenge; q_i normalized to k+1 coefficients and absorbed before r*
- prove() returns Result instead of panicking on unsupported circuits
- convert: require every output gate (R1CS constraint) to be zero, not only
  gate 0; Input carries output/input values
